From c64836a0ead90b3ba3bb5139d6a41ab2abad50c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 00:21:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/43] test(chexc): red-first groups for aliases, assumption
 imports, conversions, adapt

aliases/ (4): tuple-alias capability lists incl. nested aliases and captures
clauses; element-validation and cyclic-alias negatives.
assume/ (3 + support pkg): @AssumeThrows imposing a list on calls into an
unchecked dependency, bare form = Exception, unhandled-assumption negative.
conversions/ (4): Convertible boundary synthesis with cause chaining; exact-From
and no-chaining negatives; ambiguity negative; rule 1 priority + rule 6 captures
never converting.
adapt/ (2): adapt<I>(x) capturing an implementation's requirements; missing
capability and non-applicable backing type negatives.

Red state: 11/13 fail as expected (2 negatives pass vacuously on existing errors).
Conversions and adapt will be implemented on separate branches per author ruling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
